{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>For you shall serve….</b> Behold, these instances of כִּי serve in the place of אֲשֶׁר, and so in many places. And this is the sense of אִי — which is one of four senses in which כִּי serves. And we also find in many places that אִם serves in the sense of אֲשֶׁר, as in ״וְאִם תַּקְרִיב מִנְחַת בִּכּוּרִים״ (Leviticus 2), which is an obligation."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:13.847209642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}